 "title": "Metabolic Pathways and Genetic Relationships in Yeast",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the genetic and metabolic relationships in yeast, particularly focusing on the gene MET17 and its deletion mutant met17Δ. The yeast BY4741 is closely related to FY4, and both are connected to the gene HSU1, which has a pleiotropic role in sulfate utilization and a weak activity in sulfide reduction. The gene MET17 catalyzes the conversion of homocysteine to methionine, while its deletion mutant met17Δ exhibits inefficient sulfide assimilation and requires supplementation with NaHS. The cluster also explores the metabolic pathways involving homocysteine, hydrogen sulfide, and sulfide, as well as the genetic relationships between various yeast strains and genes.",
